* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact artefacts. These are never normalised, because their value
# IS their bytes: a digest is compared against them, or a signature is
# verified over them, and `text=auto` silently rewriting CRLF to LF
# changes both.
#
# This is not hypothetical. The embedded Trusted List
# (internal/trust/tsl/seed/TSL-RS.xml) is published by the Ministry with
# CRLF line endings; `text=auto` normalised them at commit time, so the
# committed seed hashed to d83bac89... instead of the 3f574484... printed
# in the Official Gazette and pinned by seedSHA256 — a byte-different
# copy of a semantically identical document, and a red CI for a phase.
# See docs/decisions.md D-107.
#
# `-text` means: store and check out verbatim, on every platform.
internal/trust/tsl/seed/TSL-RS.xml   -text
testdata/golden/**                   -text
testdata/pdfs/*.pdf                  -text
testdata/certs/*.der                 -text
internal/pades/appearance/*.flate    -text
internal/pades/appearance/*.ttf      -text
internal/pades/render/*.ttf          -text
internal/ui/assets/icon.ico          -text
internal/ui/assets/webview2/*.dll    -text
assets/*.png                         -text

# Fuzz seed corpora. Go's own format is one Go string literal per line and
# it is read literally; a CRLF checkout on Windows makes every entry a
# parse error at the point a crashing input is supposed to be replayed,
# which is the one moment it must not be.
internal/**/testdata/fuzz/**         -text
